# PowerShell coverage exclusions for the xp-gate pre-commit hook.
#
# One glob per line. Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# Matched source files are removed from Pester's -CodeCoverage path list.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# The gate measures LINE coverage across every *.ps1 in the repo. Some scripts
# cannot be instrumented by a unit-test runner at all; counting them as 0%
# permanently caps the achievable percentage, so the 80% threshold becomes
# unsatisfiable no matter how good the suite is.
#
# setup.ps1 is the motivating case:
#   - Its only logic lives in `function Main`, which ends in `exit 0` / `exit 1`.
#   - Pester's coverage instrumentation only observes the CURRENT process, so the
#     script must be dot-sourced and Main invoked in-process to be measured.
#   - Invoking Main in-process terminates the Pester host mid-run. This was
#     verified: it aborts the whole suite with
#     "MethodException: 找不到"Add"的参数计数为"1"的重载" and silently drops the
#     remaining tests (109 passed -> 66 passed, 18 "failed").
#   - Running it in a child process works and IS covered by a real end-to-end
#     test, but that contributes 0 instrumented lines by definition.
# So setup.ps1 is exercised (by tests) yet structurally unmeasurable. Excluding
# it keeps the threshold meaningful instead of gaming it.
#
# Do NOT add files here merely because they are hard to test. Everything else in
# references/scripts/ is instrumentable and expected to be covered; system-level
# branches (ACL fallbacks, HKLM mutation, restore points) belong in the
# admin-environment integration runs described in AGENTS.md.
setup.ps1
